<title>FRANCE: Sidel raised to &quot;overweight&quot; by Cheuvreux.</title>
<headline>Sidel raised to &quot;overweight&quot; by Cheuvreux.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French stockbroker Cheuvreux de Virieux raised its share recommendation on Monday for French packaging equipment maker Sidel to &quot;overweight&quot; from &quot;hold&quot;, according to fund managers.</p>
<p>Sidel shares were up 4.41 percent at 414.4 after the company reported a 23.7 percent rise in order book value, which overshadowed a 15.8 percent decline in 1996 sales.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
